# Cypress tests in Fernly

## 1. Queries

Prefer Testing Library order: `findByRole`, then `findByLabelText`, then `findByText`. Do not target CSS modules or raw tags.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — QuantityStepper.cy.tsx
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).click();

// ❌ BAD
cy.get('button.QuantityStepper-module__button').last().click();
```

## 2. States

Assert `disabled`, `checked`, or values on the element you already found. Chaining `.should('be.disabled')` on `findByRole` often fails with “Unable to find…”, which looks like a broken locator when the real issue is state.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Decrease quantity' }).then(($el) =>
  expect($el, '− at minimum quantity').to.be.disabled,
);

// ❌ BAD — QuantityStepper.cy.tsx (misleading failure at stock limit)
cy.findByRole('button', { name: 'Increase quantity' }).should('be.disabled');
```

## 3. Waiting

Never sleep for a fixed time. Wait on an intercept alias or on something the user can see.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — UI test with mocked API
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants*', { fixture: 'plants/browse-page.json' }).as('plants');
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait('@plants');
cy.findByRole('heading', { name: /plants/i });

// ❌ BAD
cy.visit('/');
cy.wait(500);
```

## 4. Data

Component tests pass props in the mount. UI tests load responses from `web/cypress/fixtures/` — one file per scenario (positive, negative, edge).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — component
cy.mount(<QuantityStepper value={2} max={5} onChange={onChange} />);

// ✅ GOOD — UI
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants/pl-snake', { fixture: 'plants/snake-plant.json' }).as('plant');

// ❌ BAD — inline huge JSON in the spec
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/plants', { body: { items: [/* … */] } });
```

## 5. Mocks

Stub only `/api/*` with `cy.intercept` and an alias. Never stub the page bundle or `window.fetch` globally.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/cart', { fixture: 'cart/signed-in-empty.json' }).as('cart');

// ❌ BAD
cy.intercept('GET', '/', { fixture: 'pages/browse.html' });
```

## 6. Tags

Exactly one level tag per test: `{ tags: '@component' }` or `{ tags: '@ui' }`. Add `@known-bug` only for a confirmed product bug; CI excludes it via `grepTags=-@known-bug`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — QuantityStepper.cy.tsx
it('disables − at the minimum', { tags: '@component' }, () => { /* … */ });

// ❌ BAD
it('disables − at the minimum', { tags: ['@component', '@ui'] }, () => { /* … */ });
```

## 7. App code

Do not change `web/src` to green a test. If the test matches `docs/PRODUCT.md`, record it in `FINDINGS.md` (see F-01: + enabled at stock limit).

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD — FINDINGS.md evidence -->
- **Evidence:** web/cypress/component/QuantityStepper.cy.tsx, "disables + at the stock limit"

<!-- ❌ BAD — “fixing” QuantityStepper.tsx value > max → value >= max without a product decision -->
```

## 8. Evidence

Label what you actually did: **executed** (test run), **inspected** (browser or code read), or **not yet tested**.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD — FINDINGS.md -->
- **Evidence:** … failing test … (executed: npm run cy:component)

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
- **Evidence:** probably wrong because we saw it once in the shop (inspected only, stated as proven)
```
